@startuml 12_Receive_Message

title 12. When Message Is Received

participant "Sender Client" as Sender
participant "WebSocket" as WS
participant "Recipient Client" as Client
participant "Memory Cache" as Memory
participant "Crypto Layer" as Crypto
participant "UI Component" as UI
actor "Recipient User" as User

Sender -> WS: Message sent\n(via flow 11)
activate WS

WS -> Client: New message event\n{message_id, encrypted_content, token_version: "v_1.3.5"}
activate Client
deactivate WS

Client -> Memory: Get token "v_1.3.5"
activate Memory

alt Token in memory
    Memory --> Client: token (plaintext)
    deactivate Memory
    note right of Client
      Latest token typically
      already in memory
    end note
    
    Client -> Crypto: Decrypt message
    activate Crypto
    note right of Crypto
      plaintext = Decrypt(
        encrypted_content,
        token
      )
    end note
    Crypto --> Client: plaintext message
    deactivate Crypto
    
    Client -> Memory: Cache decrypted message
    activate Memory
    note right of Memory
      Store in memory for display
      NOT in persistent storage
      
      Cleared on:
      - Logout
      - Browser close
      - Conversation exit
    end note
    Memory --> Client: Cached
    deactivate Memory
    
    Client -> UI: Update message list
    activate UI
    UI --> User: Display new message
    deactivate UI
    
else Token NOT in memory
    Memory --> Client: NOT FOUND
    deactivate Memory
    
    note right of Client
      Rare case: message arrived
      before token was loaded
    end note
    
    Client -> Client: Fetch token "v_1.3.5"
    note right of Client
      Follow "Fetch Conversation Data"
      flow (Diagram 08)
      - Check localStorage
      - Fetch from server if needed
    end note
    
    Client -> Client: Token retrieved
    
    Client -> Crypto: Decrypt message
    activate Crypto
    Crypto --> Client: plaintext message
    deactivate Crypto
    
    Client -> Memory: Cache decrypted message
    activate Memory
    Memory --> Client: Cached
    deactivate Memory
    
    Client -> UI: Update message list
    activate UI
    UI --> User: Display new message
    deactivate UI
end

deactivate Client

note over Sender, User
  Real-time flow:
  1. Sender encrypts with token
  2. Server relays encrypted content
  3. Recipient decrypts with same token
  4. Display immediately if token cached
  5. Brief delay if token needs fetching
  
  ✅ E2EE maintained throughout
  ✅ Server never sees plaintext
end note

@enduml
